        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-26T13:53:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’ve been dwelling on this for a… uh, while, and thought I’d start a conversation to see where it goes. I thought about hijacking <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/the-joy-of-discovery-6239\">Braithwhite’s Joy of Discovery thread</a>, but decided both would be better served on their own.</p>\n<p>I personally love to see how things unfold. I'm not one to poke and prod. I love to see how artists (in this case, the Greater Than Games folks) choose to reveal their secrets. As a game master, et al, I'm very interested in that process. I'm intrigued by the results, but I'm not generally one to want to dig into something (unless there's a personal connection).</p>\n<p>(Primarily, it's a matter of time: I consciously prioritize how I spend my time, and other things are usually higher on the list.)</p>\n<p>Other folks love to ask, love to investigate. (In my opinion, Braithwhite, you are definitely one of the most insightful and imaginative investigators in this community!  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/+1.png?v=9\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\"> ) To me, their theories and discoveries are entertaining and fun, but I'm generally not someone who's going to promote or contribute to such efforts. I don't think there's anything wrong with them - I just am not that kind of person.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"></p>\n<p>How do you all approach the secrets of the Sentinels 'verse? What facets do you enjoy?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>(Putting this in the Sentinels Comics area, as it's a meta conversation on the conversations we have here.)</p>",
