        "raw": "I&#39;ve been dwelling on this for a... uh, while, and thought I&#39;d start a conversation to see where it goes. I thought about hijacking <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/the-joy-of-discovery-6239\">Braithwhite&#39;s Joy of Discovery thread</a>, but decided both would be better served on their own.\n\nI personally love to see how things unfold. I&#39;m not one to poke and prod. I love to see how artists (in this case, the Greater Than Games folks) choose to reveal their secrets. As a game master, et al, I&#39;m very interested in that process. I&#39;m intrigued by the results, but I&#39;m not generally one to want to dig into something (unless there&#39;s a personal connection).\n\n(Primarily, it&#39;s a matter of time: I consciously prioritize how I spend my time, and other things are usually higher on the list.)\n\nOther folks love to ask, love to investigate. (In my opinion, Braithwhite, you are definitely one of the most insightful and imaginative investigators in this community!  :+1: ) To me, their theories and discoveries are entertaining and fun, but I&#39;m generally not someone who&#39;s going to promote or contribute to such efforts. I don&#39;t think there&#39;s anything wrong with them - I just am not that kind of person.  :slightly_smiling_face: \n\nHow do you all approach the secrets of the Sentinels &#39;verse? What facets do you enjoy?\n\n&nbsp;\n\n(Putting this in the Sentinels Comics area, as it&#39;s a meta conversation on the conversations we have here.)",
