      {
        "id": 121237,
        "name": "Braithwhite",
        "username": "Braithwhite",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/braithwhite/{size}/1854_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-26T14:20:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm a research librarian, so I typically go about things in a research-oriented fashion.</p><p>My typical process, such as it is, is to obsess about something that I don't have a solid theory on, or that has not been revealed by the GtG folks. &nbsp;For this specific discovery (the shadow), here are the steps that I took:</p><p>1. I've been trying to figure out who Heartbreaker:&nbsp;![](upload://2cRkZ9vPRf2b7PYZP1Q3qGjk0Ut.jpeg)&nbsp;is, and so I've been spending a lot of time doing color analysis, trying to reconstruct the logo on his chest, and trying to figure out what plot moments could lead to Fixer getting stabbed. &nbsp;</p><p>2. This led me to Daredevil. &nbsp;This particular pose looks very much like Bullseye being stabbed by Daredevil. &nbsp;<span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span>&nbsp; (in retaliation for Bullseye stabbing Elektra with one of her own sai, and its hard to see, but Daredevil is using a sai here.)</p><p>3. So I started analyzing the relationships between Fixer, The Chairman, and the Operative in that context. &nbsp;</p><p>4. I did a very close zoom of Heartbreaker's neck (no pic for that one, sorry), and it looks like he's got a something purple around his neck, with a silver pin in it. &nbsp;Which seemed odd, given his color scheme of grey and maroon.&nbsp;</p><p>5. I thought that it might be a tie, and I wondered what kind of tie the Chairman was wearing- it seemed like a long shot, but why not check?</p><p>6. So I looked at the Chairman's small art card, and noticed the shadow. &nbsp;I couldn't see it super well, so got out the big one (also, the Chairman isn't wearing a purple tie, its grey. &nbsp;Which may or may not mean anything.) &nbsp;The big villain card cuts off the bottom of the artwork, which shows the Chairman looking at his pocket watch, but it gives a wider shot, revealing more of the shadow. &nbsp;Which I noticed was human shaped. &nbsp;</p><p>7. So I started comparing the Shadow to current hero outlines, and it doesn't match any of them. &nbsp;I have since started to match it against various villain outlines, but so far no matches either.</p><p>8. With this knowledge, I've started to go back and think about the Operative/Fixer/Chairman dynamic again.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
