        "id": 121238,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-26T22:36:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Braithwhite\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/braithwhite/48/1854_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Braithwhite:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"8\">\n<li>With this knowledge, I've started to go back and think about the Operative/Fixer/Chairman dynamic again.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I lurk on the forum and enjoy every little bits that gets posted and when I introduce new players to the game I complement it with bits of lore, speculations and reference.</p>\n<p>I also contribute a little in the theories when I can. Like in this case Braithwhite made me remember how fixer's/chairman mirror's to a degree the Daredevil/Kingpin dynamic. Both turn around a street-level blind superhero martial artists facing a crime lord having great impact on his city.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
